# 2026-02-14 00:33:28.739260
+You are debugging a local full-stack photo gallery application.
+
+Environment
+
+Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript
+
+Backend: Node + Express
+
+Database: SQLite with FTS table photo_search_fts
+
+Backend Port: 3001
+
+Frontend Port: 5173
+
+Vite proxy forwards /api → http://127.0.0.1:3001
+
+Current Behavior
+
+Standard search (/api/search?q=jpg) works correctly.
+
+Backend is running and responds successfully to curl.
+
+Thumbnail endpoints return 200.
+
+AI Photo Search feature does not return results in the UI.
+
+No obvious network errors for /api/search.
+
+Some /api/people routes return 404 (may be unrelated).
+
+What You Must Do
+
+Perform a full end-to-end trace of the AI Photo Search flow:
+
+Step 1 — Locate AI Search Entry Point
+
+Identify frontend component responsible for AI search.
+
+Find the exact fetch/axios call used.
+
+Confirm endpoint path and HTTP method.
+
+Step 2 — Verify Backend Route
+
+Locate corresponding Express route.
+
+Confirm:
+
+Route exists
+
+Correct HTTP verb
+
+Correct query/body parsing
+
+Returns JSON
+
+No silent failures
+
+Step 3 — Validate Database Query
+
+Confirm correct SQL query is executed.
+
+Verify correct FTS usage:
+
+MATCH clause
+
+Proper parameter binding
+
+Ensure results are returned as array.
+
+Step 4 — Validate Response Shape
+
+Confirm backend returns:
+
+{ "photos": [...] }
+
+
+Ensure frontend expects same shape.
+
+Step 5 — Check Common Failure Points
+
+Proxy misconfiguration
+
+CORS issues
+
+Missing await
+
+State not updating
+
+Conditional rendering blocking results
+
+Early return preventing display
+
+Unhandled promise rejection
+
+React hook order violations
+
+Output Required
+
+Exact root cause.
+
+Minimal, surgical fix.
+
+Unified diff patch for affected files.
+
+Clear explanation of why it failed.
+
+Confirmation that:
+
+Endpoint works via curl
+
+Frontend renders results
+
+No console errors remain
+
+Do not speculate. Trace actual execution path and fix only what is broken.

