# 2026-02-14 15:22:36.234512
+Restore/fix “AI photo search” in the Family Photo Gallery app (React/Vite frontend + Node/Express backend) and verify that frontend↔backend routing/proxying is working end-to-end in local dev on Windows.
+
+Platform
+
+Windows (PowerShell / Command Prompt)
+
+Frontend: Vite + React (dev server on http://127.0.0.1:5173)
+
+Backend: Node/Express (API on http://127.0.0.1:3001)
+
+Vite proxy configured to forward /api, /thumbnails, /photos, /display to http://127.0.0.1:3001
+
+Actions taken
+
+Confirmed backend is running (port 3001 already bound) after hitting:
+
+curl.exe http://127.0.0.1:3001/health (PowerShell warned because curl alias; used curl.exe/basic parsing guidance)
+
+Confirmed frontend proxy path works by querying the API through Vite:
+
+curl.exe http://127.0.0.1:5173/api/search?q=jpg → returned JSON { photos: [...] }
+
+Browser DevTools: await fetch("/api/search?q=jpg").then(r => r.json()) → returned photos: Array(...)
+
+Confirmed thumbnails accessible both direct and via Vite proxy:
+
+curl.exe -I http://127.0.0.1:3001/api/photos/<id>/thumbnail → 200 OK
+
+curl.exe -I http://127.0.0.1:5173/api/photos/<id>/thumbnail → 200 OK
+
+Observed backend start attempt failed with:
+
+Error: listen EADDRINUSE :::3001 (another backend instance already running)
+
+Noted frontend console/network errors for missing endpoints:
+
+GET /api/people and /api/people/unidentified returning 404
+
+favicon.ico 404
+
+Attempted to locate the frontend call site for /api/search using findstr, but ran into:
+
+incorrect directory assumptions (path C:\Users\bmilh\photo-app\frontend not found; project appears nested under photo-backend\frontend)
+
+confusing findstr output like “FINDSTR: /a ignored” (likely command formatting / quoting / PowerShell vs CMD differences)
+
+Potential pitfalls / gotchas
+
+PowerShell curl is an alias for Invoke-WebRequest; prefer curl.exe to avoid parsing prompts/warnings.
+
+EADDRINUSE on 3001 means the backend is already running; starting another instance will fail (you must stop the existing process or change the port).
+
+Vite proxy only works while Vite is running; if curl.exe http://127.0.0.1:5173/... fails to connect, the Vite dev server isn’t running or isn’t bound to 127.0.0.1:5173.
+
+404s for /api/people* indicate frontend is calling endpoints that the backend doesn’t implement (or routes are not mounted), which can break “AI/people search” features.
+
+Finding code on Windows: findstr is picky; wrong working directory or glob patterns can make it look like strings don’t exist.
+
+Current status
+
+Backend + Vite proxy are working for /api/search and thumbnails (confirmed via curl.exe and DevTools fetch).
+
+AI photo search still not working in the app UI (likely tied to missing/404 “people/AI” endpoints or the frontend calling routes that don’t exist / aren’t wired).
+
+Next debugging focus is to identify the exact failing UI feature path (e.g., “AI search” hitting /api/people... endpoints) and implement/fix the missing backend routes or update frontend to call the correct existing API routes.

