# 2026-02-15 02:01:57.287200
+You are seeing two separate symptoms that point to one root cause:
+
+CORS error
+
+502 Bad Gateway
+
+apiBase: '' in console log
+
+Let’s break this down clearly.
+
+What This Error Actually Means
+Browser Error
+No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present
+
+
+This does NOT automatically mean CORS is misconfigured.
+
+When the backend returns a 502, Cloudflare does not include your Express CORS headers.
+
+So the browser reports it as a CORS failure — but the real problem is:
+
+The backend is not responding successfully.
+
+Network Error
+GET https://api.milhizerfamilyphotos.org/api/photos... 502 (Bad Gateway)
+
+
+A 502 from Cloudflare means:
+
+Cloudflare cannot reach your backend at 127.0.0.1:3001
+
+That means one of these is true:
+
+Backend server is not running
+
+Cloudflare tunnel is not running
+
+Backend crashed
+
+Tunnel token expired
+
+Port changed
+
+Firewall blocked
+
+This is infrastructure-level, not frontend-level.
+
+The Bigger Clue
+
+From your console:
+
+[PhotoMasonry] photos loaded {count: 0, apiBase: '', sample: null}
+
+
+apiBase: ''
+
+That means:
+
+VITE_API_BASE_URL is NOT set in this build.
+
+This is the same class of issue you fixed before.
+
+From your project notes:
+
+All frontend fetch calls must prefix with import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL
+
+And:
+
+The env var is injected during CI build
+
+If it’s empty, the frontend might be falling back to a relative path or constructing the URL incorrectly.
+
+But since the request clearly shows:
+
+https://api.milhizerfamilyphotos.org/api/photos
+
+
+The base URL was probably correct at build time.
+
+So this points more strongly to:
+
+Backend / tunnel not running.
+
+How We Fixed This Previously
+
+Based on your handoff summary 
+
+Below is a compact handoff summ…
+
+Production required:
+
+Backend running on port 3001
+
+Cloudflare Tunnel running separately
+
+Firebase frontend deployed with correct env
+
+No credentials: "include"
+
+VITE_API_BASE_URL defined in production
+
+From CLAUDE.md 
+
+CLAUDE
+
+Production API:
+
+https://api.milhizerfamilyphotos.org
+
+
+Tunnel exposes:
+
+127.0.0.1:3001
+
+Most Likely Root Cause (90% Confidence)
+
+Your backend or Cloudflare tunnel is not running right now.
+
+A 502 from Cloudflare almost always means:
+
+Cloudflare cannot reach your local server.
+
+This is not a frontend bug.
+
+Immediate Diagnostic (Do This Now)
+
+On your Windows machine:
+
+Step 1 — Is backend running?
+
+Open PowerShell:
+
+netstat -ano | findstr :3001
+
+
+If nothing returns → backend is not running.
+
+Step 2 — Is tunnel running?
+
+Open PowerShell:
+
+sc query cloudflared
+
+
+OR check Task Manager for cloudflared.exe
+
+Step 3 — Test backend directly
+
+In browser, try:
+
+http://127.0.0.1:3001/health
+
+
+If that fails → backend is down.
+
+Why the CORS Message Is Misleading
+
+When Cloudflare returns 502, it does not include:
+
+Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
+
+
+So browser throws a CORS error.
+
+But the real failure is upstream connectivity.
+
+This exact thing happens constantly with Cloudflare tunnels.
+
+Summary
+
+This is NOT:
+
+React issue
+
+Envelope unwrap issue
+
+Credentials issue
+
+Firebase issue
+
+This IS:
+
+Infrastructure connectivity between:
+
+Cloudflare → Tunnel → 127.0.0.1:3001

