# 2026-02-15 02:52:58.434799
+The error:
+
+SyntaxError: The requested module './db.js' does not provide an export named 'default'
+
+
+means:
+
+Your server.js is doing this:
+
+import db from './db.js';
+
+
+But db.js does NOT have:
+
+export default ...
+
+
+So Node is correctly refusing to start.
+
+Why This Is Happening
+
+You are running:
+
+Node.js v18.12.0
+
+
+Your project is ESM ("type": "module").
+
+In ESM:
+
+If you write:
+
+import db from './db.js';
+
+
+Then db.js MUST contain:
+
+export default something;
+
+
+If instead db.js contains something like:
+
+export const db = ...
+
+
+or
+
+export function getDb() ...
+
+
+Then your import must be:
+
+import { db } from './db.js';
+
+
+or
+
+import { getDb } from './db.js';
+
+This Likely Happened Because
+
+One of these:
+
+db.js was modified
+
+A version mismatch between machines
+
+A merge overwrote export style
+
+You copied files from another branch
+
+Node version differences exposed a mismatch

# 2026-02-15 21:29:59.819414
+Root Cause
+
+In server.js you have:
+
+import db from './db.js';
+
+
+But in db.js you export this:
+
+export const db = await open(...)
+
+
+There is no default export.
+
+So Node is correct when it says:
+
+does not provide an export named 'default'
+
+The Fix (One Line)
+
+Change this line in server.js:
+
+import db from './db.js';
+
+
+to:
+
+import { db } from './db.js';
+
+
+That’s it.
+
+Why This Works
+
+db.js exports a named export:
+
+export const db = ...
+
+
+So you must import it as a named import:
+
+import { db } from './db.js';
+
+What To Do Now
+1️⃣ Edit server.js
+
+Replace the first 5 lines with:
+
+import express from 'express';
+import cors from 'cors';
+import path from 'path';
+import { fileURLToPath } from 'url';
+import { db } from './db.js';
+
+
+Only that change.
+
+2️⃣ Start backend again
+
+In:
+
+C:\Users\bmilh\photo-app\photo-backend
+
+
+Run:
+
+npm run server
+
+3️⃣ Test locally
+
+Open browser:
+
+http://127.0.0.1:3001/api/health
+
+
+If you see:
+
+{ "status": "OK", ... }
+
+
+Then backend is fixed.
+
+4️⃣ Test production
+https://api.milhizerfamilyphotos.org/api/health
+
+
+If that works → frontend will immediately start working.
+
+Why This Broke
+
+Likely:
+
+db.js was rewritten to use named exports
+
+server.js was not updated
+
+Or files came from two different versions
+
+Classic ESM mismatch.

# 2026-02-16 00:49:06.766715
+Where To Fix
+
+In your frontend:
+
+You likely have something like:
+
+const API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE || '';
+
+
+And in production, it’s blank.
+
+So it defaults to same-origin /api.
+
+That works locally.
+
+It does not work in production.
+
+Proper Production Configuration
+
+In your frontend .env.production:
+
+VITE_API_BASE=https://api.milhizerfamilyphotos.org
+
+
+Then in your API calls:
+
+const apiUrl = `${API_BASE}/api/photos/${id}/thumbnail`
+
+
+Not relative /api/....

