# 2026-02-17 01:04:40.998955
+You are a senior Python ML engineer.
+
+I have an existing local AI image tagging script (Python 3.11, CUDA PyTorch, BLIP captioning model). It:
+
+- Generates captions for images
+- Splits caption text into simple tokens
+- Inserts tokens into SQLite tables:
+    tags(name)
+    photo_tags(photo_id, tag_id, added_by)
+
+The problem:
+The current implementation stores low-quality tokens like:
+- are
+- around
+- little
+- three
+- her
+- sitting
+
+I want to upgrade the tagging logic to behave more like Google Photos.
+
+GOALS:
+
+1. Use spaCy (en_core_web_sm) for NLP parsing.
+2. Extract:
+   - Nouns (POS == NOUN or PROPN)
+   - Noun chunks (multi-word phrases like "christmas tree", "surfboard", "birthday cake")
+3. Remove:
+   - Verbs
+   - Adjectives unless part of noun chunk
+   - Stopwords
+   - Words shorter than 3 characters
+4. Deduplicate tokens.
+5. Lowercase everything.
+6. Keep both:
+   - Single nouns
+   - Multi-word noun phrases
+7. Avoid duplicate tag insertions (photo_tags already uses INSERT OR IGNORE).
+8. Keep the existing database structure untouched.
+9. Preserve GPU BLIP captioning logic exactly as-is.
+10. Keep batch arguments: --limit and --offset.
+
+OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS:
+
+- Return a FULL file replacement for tagger.py.
+- No partial snippets.
+- No commentary outside the code.
+- The script must remain runnable via:
+
+    python ai/tagger.py --limit 10 --offset 0
+
+- Must use:
+
+    import spacy
+    nlp = spacy.load("en_core_web_sm")
+
+- The script must gracefully handle:
+    - Missing image files
+    - spaCy loading errors
+    - Empty captions
+
+- Do NOT modify database schema.
+- Do NOT modify caption generation logic.
+- Only improve token extraction logic.
+
+Provide clean production-level code.
+

